# Normalise line endings on commit, check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, a worktree copied from or edited on Windows commits CRLF, and every line of the file
# reads as changed. That hides the real diff and makes an unrelated one-line edit look like a
# rewrite. core.autocrlf is a per-machine setting and cannot be relied on across three developers,
# so the rule lives in the repo instead.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files git should never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
